"For integers $q\\geq 2$ and $\\delta\\geq 1$, let $c_{\\delta,q}$ be the smallest constant such that every finite digraph $D$ with minimum in-degree at least $\\delta$ contains a $q$-kernel of size at most $c_{\\delta,q}|V(D)|$. A **$q$-kernel** is an independent set $Q\\subseteq V(D)$ from which every vertex is reachable by a directed path of length at most $q$.\n\n**Exact asymptotic bound conjecture.** For all $\\delta\\geq 1$ and $q\\geq 3$,\n\n$$\nc_{\\delta,q}=\\frac{1}{\\delta+1}.\n$$\n\nThe paper establishes the lower bound $1/(\\delta+1)\\leq c_{\\delta,q}$ and an upper bound of $1/(\\lfloor\\sqrt{\\delta+1}\\rfloor+1)$ for $q\\geq 3$, while equality is proved when $q\\geq \\lceil 3\\delta/2\\rceil+1$. The conjecture remains unresolved in the remaining parameter ranges."